# Code Structure & Maintenance Standards

## **CRITICAL: Directory Structure Enforcement**

### **Root Level Organization**

```
logistics/
├── .cursor/rules/         # AI assistance rules (this file)
├── .husky/               # Git hooks for code quality
├── backend/              # All microservices
│   ├── api-gateway/      # Request routing & middleware
│   ├── auth-service/     # Authentication & authorization
│   ├── user-service/     # User management
│   ├── shipment-service/ # Shipment tracking
│   ├── support-service/  # Customer support
│   └── platform-service/ # Platform integrations
├── frontend/             # Next.js application
├── shared/               # Cross-service utilities
├── docs/                 # Technical documentation
├── memory-bank/          # Project context & intelligence
└── scripts/              # Build & deployment scripts
```

### **Backend Service Structure**

Every backend service MUST follow this structure:

```
service-name/
├── prisma/
│   ├── schema.prisma     # Database schema
│   └── migrations/       # Database migrations
├── src/                  # Source code (if using TypeScript)
│   ├── controllers/      # Route handlers
│   ├── middleware/       # Custom middleware
│   ├── models/          # Data models & business logic
│   ├── routes/          # Route definitions
│   ├── services/        # Business services
│   └── utils/           # Service-specific utilities
├── tests/               # Test files
├── .env.example         # Environment variables template
├── Dockerfile           # Container configuration
├── package.json         # Dependencies & scripts
└── server.js           # Entry point
```

## **File Naming & Organization Rules**

### **MANDATORY: Consistent Naming**

- **Controllers**: `[entity]Controller.js` (e.g., `userController.js`)
- **Routes**: `[entity].js` (e.g., `users.js`, `auth.js`)
- **Middleware**: `[function]Middleware.js` (e.g., `authMiddleware.js`)
- **Services**: `[entity]Service.js` (e.g., `userService.js`)
- **Models**: `[Entity].js` (PascalCase, e.g., `User.js`)
- **Utilities**: `[function].js` (camelCase, e.g., `dateUtils.js`)

### **Frontend File Organization**

```
frontend/src/
├── app/                 # Next.js 14 App Router
│   ├── (auth)/         # Route groups
│   ├── dashboard/      # Dashboard pages
│   └── api/           # API routes
├── components/
│   ├── ui/            # Atomic components (Button, Input)
│   ├── forms/         # Form components
│   ├── layout/        # Layout components
│   └── features/      # Feature-specific components
├── hooks/             # Custom React hooks
├── lib/               # Utilities & configurations
├── types/             # TypeScript type definitions
└── styles/            # Styling files
```

## **CRITICAL: Code Quality Standards**

### **Import Organization**

Always organize imports in this order:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Import order
// 1. Node.js built-ins
import path from "path";
import fs from "fs";

// 2. External libraries
import express from "express";
import { PrismaClient } from "@prisma/client";

// 3. Internal modules (absolute imports first)
import { authMiddleware } from "../middleware/authMiddleware.js";
import { validateUser } from "../validation/userValidation.js";

// 4. Relative imports (closest first)
import "./styles.css";
```

### **Function & Component Organization**

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Function organization
// 1. Main exported function/component
export function UserController() {
  // Main logic
}

// 2. Helper functions (not exported)
function validateUserInput(data) {
  // Helper logic
}

// 3. Constants & configurations
const USER_ROLES = ["Admin", "Client", "Operations"];
```

