## **Error Handling & Logging Standards**

### **MANDATORY: Consistent Error Classes**

Create custom error classes for each service:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Custom error classes
class ValidationError extends Error {
  constructor(message, field = null) {
    super(message);
    this.name = "ValidationError";
    this.statusCode = 400;
    this.code = "VALIDATION_ERROR";
    this.field = field;
  }
}

class NotFoundError extends Error {
  constructor(resource, id) {
    super(`${resource} with ID ${id} not found`);
    this.name = "NotFoundError";
    this.statusCode = 404;
    this.code = "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND";
    this.resource = resource;
    this.resourceId = id;
  }
}
```

### **Audit Logging Requirements**

All CRUD operations MUST be logged:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Audit logging
async function createUser(userData, requestContext) {
  const user = await prisma.user.create({ data: userData });

  // Audit log entry
  await auditLogger.log({
    action: "USER_CREATED",
    resourceType: "User",
    resourceId: user.id,
    userId: requestContext.user?.id,
    ipAddress: requestContext.ipAddress,
    userAgent: requestContext.userAgent,
    metadata: {
      userEmail: user.email,
      userRole: user.role,
    },
  });

  return user;
}
```

## **Security Standards**

### **Input Sanitization**

Always sanitize user inputs:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Input sanitization
import validator from "validator";
import { escape } from "html-escaper";

function sanitizeUserInput(input) {
  return {
    email: validator.normalizeEmail(input.email),
    name: escape(input.name.trim()),
    phone: input.phone.replace(/\D/g, ""), // Remove non-digits
  };
}
```

### **Password Security**

Use bcrypt for password hashing:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Password hashing
import bcrypt from "bcrypt";

async function hashPassword(plainPassword) {
  const saltRounds = 12;
  return await bcrypt.hash(plainPassword, saltRounds);
}

async function verifyPassword(plainPassword, hashedPassword) {
  return await bcrypt.compare(plainPassword, hashedPassword);
}
```

